      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A total of 1139 representatives of various groups of the USSR population (indigenous inhabitants of Chukotsk and the Altai, migrants to Chukotsk living there for various periods of time and citizens of Novosibirsk) was studied to determine whether the assay of Lp (a)-lipoproteins, a normal genetic marker, can be used as a novel diagnostic test for coronary heart disease. Coronary heart disease was shown to be correlated with the presence of Lp (a)-lipoprotein, with X2 being statistically significant."},
